commit 934e36e044d39bf9eaf01b28c7bf815089860706
Author: David Harris <David_Harris@hmc.edu>
Date:   Tue Sep 15 20:56:57 2026 -0700

    Add Zabha support
    
    Zabha adds byte and halfword AMOs. Most of the plumbing was already
    width-generic: the byte mask is computed from the size field, the
    misaligned check is a case on size, and the subword read and write paths
    are shared with ordinary loads and stores.
    
    Two changes were needed. The decode splits the atomic width check in two
    so the AMO forms accept funct3 of 000 and 001 while lr and sc stay at word
    and doubleword, since Zabha does not add narrow reservations. The AMO ALU
    narrows both comparands to the access width before the shared word
    comparator; the memory operand arrives sign-extended from the subword
    read, which is wrong for the unsigned min and max forms, so both operands
    are re-extended from their raw low bits per the signedness bit.
    
    Enabled on rv64gc and rv32gc.
    
    Verified on rv64gc: all 18 Zabha arch tests pass, along with the 22
    existing Zaamo and Zalrsc tests and the 48 Zimop and Zcmop tests. Lint is
    clean on every config.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

